(1. A member sits on a public company's board and buys the stock before a vote she knows will pass. What should she do instead?) Tj
0 -16 Td
(A. Trade only after the vote is public and information is no longer MNPI.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(B. Trade immediately for clients because the vote is nearly certain.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(C. Tell her largest client so they can trade first.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(D. Hedge with options in a personal account only.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Answer: A) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Explanation: Board knowledge of a pending vote is material nonpublic information; she must wait until it is public under II\(A\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
ET
endstream
