48 720 Td
(4. A private-wealth manager recommends a concentrated stock position because it is the manager's own largest holding. The loyalty problem is which of these?) Tj
0 -16 Td
(A. Failing to put the client's interests ahead of the manager's own.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(B. Using material nonpublic information about the holding.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(C. Misrepresenting the stock's historical dividend record.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(D. Failing to sit for the next CFA exam window.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Answer: A) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Explanation: III\(A\) requires loyalty, prudence, and care; recommending a position because it benefits the manager violates that duty.) Tj
0 -16 Td
ET
